  "title": "BCCWJ-MEG",
  "description": "BCCWJ-MEG contains magnetoencephalography recordings from 35 native Japanese speakers who read Japanese newspaper articles word by word. It is one part of the BCCWJ-Brain collection, which also includes fMRI and EEG datasets acquired from separate participant groups with the same stimuli, allowing cross-modality comparison of language processing. Raw data, T1-weighted anatomical images, and preprocessed derivatives (CALM-filtered, ICA-cleaned, and evoked files) are provided.",
  "methods_description": "Continuous MEG was recorded with a 200-channel axial gradiometer whole-head system (RICOH) in a shielded room at 1,000 Hz. Twenty newspaper articles were presented word by word using RSVP in PsychoPy, with 500 ms per word followed by a 500 ms blank. Preprocessing used MNE-Python and Eelbrain, including CALM noise reduction, ICA-based ocular artifact removal, 0.1-40 Hz bandpass filtering, epoching from -100 to 1000 ms, and downsampling to 200 Hz. T1-weighted images were defaced with PyDeface.",
